Hi team,

During service degradation, repeated attempts can inflate volume and obscure =
the number of customers actually affected.

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use March 2023 as the new evidence point rather =
than recycling the earlier conclusion. Several teams are reporting more faile=
d or retried activity than they expected, but they do not agree on the cause.

Can you test these explanations rather than choosing one at the start?
- channel switching follows a timeout
- automatic retry and human retry are being mixed
- customers retry the same action within minutes

The decision is how monitoring should count affected customers and when retry=
 controls should activate. Please give us a working Excel file with the excep=
tion population and clear columns.

You should be able to build the evidence from transaction-level timestamps, c=
hannels, amounts, statuses and error context; ATM attempts, host responses, P=
IN attempts, blocked-card state and latency. Without application session IDs,=
 use account, amount, channel and time proximity as an explicit matching heur=
istic.

